From: Devin <devin@cognition.ai>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: ppe: skip MAC check for PPPoE flows

Adapted from orangeyoo/XR1710G-OpenWrt-iStoreOS-Community
9999-32-net-airoha-ppe-pppoe-skip-mac-check.

For PPPoE flows the nf_flow_table offload path (FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_DIRECT)
does not emit FLOW_ACTION_MANGLE/FLOW_ACT_MANGLE_HDR_TYPE_ETH, so
data.eth.h_dest/h_source remain zero.  The PPE hardware resolves the
outer L2 header from the physical egress port and the PPPoE session ID
(already stored in data.pppoe.sid via FLOW_ACTION_PPPOE_PUSH), so the
MAC check is incorrect for this path and must be skipped.

Signed-off-by: Devin <devin@cognition.ai>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -2803,8 +2803,17 @@ static int airoha_ppe_flow_offload_repl
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (!is_valid_ether_addr(data.eth.h_source) ||
-	    !is_valid_ether_addr(data.eth.h_dest)) {
+	/*
+	 * For PPPoE flows the nf_flow_table offload path
+	 * (FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_DIRECT) does not emit
+	 * FLOW_ACTION_MANGLE/FLOW_ACT_MANGLE_HDR_TYPE_ETH, so
+	 * data.eth.h_dest/h_source remain zero.  The PPE hardware resolves
+	 * the outer L2 header from the egress port and the PPPoE session
+	 * ID, so the MAC check must be skipped for this path.
+	 */
+	if (!data.pppoe.num &&
+	    (!is_valid_ether_addr(data.eth.h_source) ||
+	     !is_valid_ether_addr(data.eth.h_dest))) {
 		airoha_ppe_drop_inc(eth->ppe, AIROHA_PPE_DROP_INVALID_MAC);
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
